+# Head15 v4 bounded record-boundary diagnostic source design
+
+The v3 actual runtime ended at the first top reset predicate at 6666 ps, before any command. Fourteen owner reset messages print zero records and zero counts; no wrapper or successful top witness ran before termination. Top raw fields and individual predicate results were not printed. Root cause is unresolved. This design authorizes source preparation only and preserves all v3 evidence.
+
+## Fresh source and preserved preimage
+
+Work only in this fresh sibling. Archive exact v3 maintained testbench/runner/generator/binder source files, source packet, design, literal source diff and first-failure evidence identities before copying. Record each original/archive path, bytes, mode and SHA. Do not copy or modify production, generated numerical RTL, DAT, installed libraries, numerical images, prepared pages or any prior build/run. Reference them by frozen identity. v3 source/results.md and all sealed packets remain frozen.
+
+Make a new source/results.md that explicitly says source-only and unmeasured. New top/generator must agree. The established 119-bit record, owner, packing, numerical control and hold/debt/association checks are preserved exactly. No changes to accepted AXI endpoints, clock, reset sequence, command count, expected bytes, watchdog, selected qkv1 port4, or numerical status checks. At this stage do not replace $isunknown, convert arrays, alter output logic/wire types, add resets/deposits or change the observed connection topology to make the failure disappear.
+
+## Full-testbench instrumentation candidate
+
+Before any record reset predicate can issue a fatal at the first settled negative edge, obtain a complete central bounded diagnostic snapshot for all seven ports. Use explicit constant-index emitted statements for every port so diagnostic collection itself cannot hide a variable-index expression issue. The generator may produce these statements from a fixed seven-entry port-name map.
+
+For each port print owner .accepted_r_record and .r_count at both monitor instances, wrapper dut_monitor_accepted_r_record and ram_monitor_accepted_r_record, wrapper output ram_accepted_r_record and ram_r_count, and constant-index top array record/count. Also print the same top element reached through the existing variable p loop. Print records and counts in hexadecimal and binary as raw four-state values; include port index, simulation time, clock/reset values and seen-reset-posedge flag. This limited hierarchical read is diagnostic only, never a numerical authority or a replacement for the explicit record interface; no old internal r_accept scalar may be used. Bind every hierarchical name to the actual frozen named-instance map.
+
+For each top record/count pair print independently: record case-nonzero, count case-nonzero, per-field reduction-X detection ((^field) === 1'bx), per-field $isunknown, original $isunknown on the variable-index concatenation, original expression at a literal constant index, and $isunknown on a local151-bit packed snapshot assigned from the same fields. Print the packed snapshot raw bits too. Evaluate and print diagnostics before the preserved original predicate. Do not merge its logical terms into a replacement authority. Keep X/Z checks strict. At later first-R witnesses, retain existing exact ordinal/address/beat/RID/last checks; diagnostic output remains bounded to reset and first-R per port per reset.
+
+Diagnostics must finish before any sibling record reset diagnostic fatal, independent of active-region block ordering. A practical candidate is a centralized top diagnostic task called immediately before the unchanged top predicate, together with wrapper reset-fatal diagnostics routed through the same top coordinator or deferred only within the diagnostic-check execution until a `diagnostic_snapshot_complete` flag for that exact negative edge is set. Do not delay clock/reset, transaction processing or state update. The owner posedge reset assertion already passed in v3; retain its behavior. If coordination would alter a predicate or cause a scheduling dependency, prefer a single top task that reads all three boundaries and directly invokes all preserved wrapper and top record-reset checks in their original same-negedge observation phase; record this exact assertion-placement-only change. Do not modify numerical/transaction check timing. Provide a source-level explanation and literal diff for independent review; no claim that this instrumentation alone fixes the fault.
+
+## Minimal no-DUT same-connection probe
+
+Prepare a separate probe under diagnostic/ with no production/generated DUT, no AXI memory endpoint, no fixture/oracle and no host numerical calls. Reproduce exactly the record-owner output logic[118:0] and32-bit count, named connection to wrapper internal logic, continuous assignment to wrapper output logic, and connection to a seven-element top unpacked array with the same declaration direction and range as v3. Preserve the direct count path. Use the same1ns/1ps precision, clock half-period and reset-positive-edge then next-negative-edge observation as v3. Emit a source equivalence table referencing exact v3 declarations/connection lines. Mock owner behavior is explicitly synthetic: zero both fields on reset, then write a deterministic known119-bit record with valid=1 and ordinal matching count through one local owner. It has no numerical or AXI acceptance meaning.
+
+Separate this probe into a diagnostic collection phase and an assertion phase so all raw owner/wrapper/top values and all expression variants are printed before any failure. Include the unchanged original variable-index predicate as the baseline under test; print its boolean result without permitting it to truncate diagnostic collection. Preserve a final nonzero exit if any required known-value or correspondence assertion fails. Known-value patterns must include all-zero reset, first valid record with nontrivial address/beat/len/size/IDs/last fields, and a subsequent reset. All seven ports must use distinct nonzero values after reset, preventing accidental cross-port aliasing. Add an explicit bounded X injection at the synthetic owner on one separately labelled phase to verify the alternate unknown detectors reject unknown data; this is test-only stimulus and must never be carried into the Head15 testbench. End after a statically enumerated finite schedule, e.g. no more than32clockcycles, with a finite watchdog. No random stimulus, open-ended polling or variable user input.
+
+Provide dormant compile/elaboration/runtime commands using the same installed2025.2 compiler/simulator/library identities. No command runs under this source release. Source proof must enumerate exact cycle schedule, maximum prints and expected per-phase values. Actual simulator outputs, tool defect conclusions, successful build and even syntax acceptance remain unmeasured until a separate independent execution gate.
+
+## Acceptance boundaries
+
+Reviewer first checks preimages, unchanged control tail, generator consistency, raw-before-fatal coverage, exact connection equivalence and finite probe schedule. Only then may a distinct one-attempt small-memory/short-wall compile-and-probe gate be issued. Root schedules that tool execution in the sole heavy slot. Full Head15 rebuild and runtime remain held until minimal evidence explains which data/expression boundary differs and a separately reviewed correction or justified next diagnostic exists. No retry or automatic quota increase. Any later corrective implementation gets a fresh source packet; do not amend this or earlier sealed evidence.
